  "summary": "Validates the announced coin count in AssumeUTXO snapshot metadata against the unique UTXO count produced during import, and rejects transaction groups specifying zero coins during deserialization. Content hash checks take precedence over coin count errors.",
  "problem": "AssumeUTXO snapshot loading verifies content hash but does not check the metadata's announced coin count against the unique UTXOs imported into the chainstate. A malformed snapshot with duplicate records collapses outpoints into single entries, matching the serialized UTXO hash while reporting an inflated count in `loadtxoutset`. Furthermore, empty transaction groups (zero coins) pass deserialization without advancing the coin counter, which bypasses the loop interrupt check and can delay node shutdown.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Repeated outpoints collapse into one coin, so a snapshot can repeat every record, announce the doubled count, and still match the committed UTXO hash. loadtxoutset then reports the inflated count as coins_loaded.'",
    "Commit e8e8cbcaa2: 'Snapshots generated by dumptxoutset already contain only nonempty groups.'"
  ],
